{title: Count Your Blessings}
{artist: Johnson Oatman Jr. / Edwin O. Excell}
{genre: Hymn, Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 96}
{time: 4/4}
{hymnal: 새찬송가 429장}
{title_ko: 세상 모든 풍파 너를 흔들어}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]When upon life's billows you are [D]tempest tossed
When you are dis[G]couraged, thinking [D]all is lost
[G]Count your many [C]blessings, name them [G]one by one
And it [A7]will sur[D]prise you what the [G]Lord hath done
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Count your blessings, [D]name them one by [G]one
Count your blessings, [D]see what God hath [G]done
Count your [G]blessings, [C]name them one by [G]one
Count your [A7]many [D]blessings, see what [G]God hath done
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Are you ever burdened with a [D]load of care?
Does the cross seem [G]heavy you are [D]called to bear?
[G]Count your many [C]blessings, every [G]doubt will fly
And you [A7]will be [D]singing as the [G]days go by
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]When you look at others with their [D]lands and gold
Think that Christ has [G]promised you His [D]wealth untold
[G]Count your many [C]blessings, wealth can [G]never buy
Your re[A7]ward in [D]heaven, nor your [G]home on high
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]So, amid the conflict, whether [D]great or small
Do not be dis[G]couraged, God is [D]over all
[G]Count your many [C]blessings, angels [G]will attend
Help and [A7]comfort [D]give you to your [G]journey's end
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
